## Interactions

- The sign-in methods match Nexus: Passkey, GitHub and LINUX DO each simulate about a second of system verification or provider authorization, then move on; email is checked first, then shows Magic Link sent, and I opened the link (demo) finishes signing in. Continue offline skips the workspace step, and the last step notes that cross-device sync is unavailable.
- Continue works only once the step is satisfied (a sign-in method, a named space or an accepted invitation, file access granted), and the footer says what is missing; Back and the finished steps on the left both go back. When you change steps, focus moves to the new step's heading.
- The summon shortcut can be recorded: press Record, then a combination that includes ⌘, ⌃ or ⌥; Esc cancels. Combinations the browser keeps, such as ⌘W or ⌘T, are refused with a hint. The recorded shortcut carries over to the last step and the live preview.
- Every permission waits for you to press Allow access: about 1.2 seconds stand in for the system dialog, then it reads Granted. Screen recording is refused the first time, the row offers Open System Settings, and a second press grants it with a Takes effect after a restart (sample) note.
- Once in view only the entrance plays: the logo and title draw once, the beam on the Passkey button fades in after about 0.9 s and the tagline sweeps once at 1.4 s. Watch the flow signs in, joins the team, flashes the recording ring on the shortcut, then stops at permissions with a note that the template never grants them for you. A click or any key inside the template stops it; with reduced motion on it jumps straight to permissions, with no beam and no sweep.
- On the last step, with focus inside the template, press your summon shortcut and the big keycaps light up with it; once summoned a miniature CoreBox pops up. Simulate the press does the same. Wide (≥ 960px) enlarges the brand rail and type, and ≥ 1200px adds the live preview on the right; narrow (< 640px) folds the brand rail into a row across the top and the step bar keeps only its markers.

## Adapting it

- Real sign-in: replace the timer in `signIn()` with the Nexus OAuth redirect or a WebAuthn call, and the Magic Link with the real mail endpoint. Do not add a password field: Nexus has no password sign-in, and a password field that leaves the page after submit also triggers the browser's save-password prompt.
- Real permissions: read the state from the system (Privacy & Security on macOS, the privacy settings on Windows) and check again after Allow access raises the system dialog. Grants start from the user's click only; onboarding never requests them on its own.
- The entrance effects (TxTuffLogoStroke with `once`, TxKeyframeStrokeText, TxGlowText with `:repeat="false"`) all play when they mount, so mount them once they are visible and change their `key` to replay. TxBorderBeam's rotating family (`sm`, `md`, `line`) has no reduced-motion fallback, so pass `:active="false"` then; its `theme` defaults to `dark` and `auto` follows the system rather than the site, so pass the current theme explicitly.
- TxSteps emits nothing: clicking a step only changes its own internal state. To go back, put a native `@click` on TxStep, check that the target step is finished, and give `clickable` to finished steps only.
